## Email Protocols
Several protocols work behind the scenes to deliver messages, each with a specific functional role.

### Sending (Outbound)
* **SMTP (Simple Mail Transfer Protocol):** Think of this as the **Courier**. Its only job is to move the email from the sender to the server, and then from one server to another. It "pushes" the mail toward its destination.

### Receiving (Inbound)
* **POP3 (Post Office Protocol v3):** Think of this as a **Physical Mailbox**. You go to the post office, take your letters out, and bring them home. Once they are at your house, they are no longer at the post office (deleted from the server).
* **IMAP (Internet Message Access Protocol):** Think of this as **Cloud Storage**. You can access your mail from any device. If you delete a message on your phone, it disappears from your laptop because the "master copy" remains synced on the server.

